     1	# Scene queries and allocation admission
     2	
     3	This crate ports safe scene selection and explicit memory-capacity accounting.
     4	`bounds_query` and `hit_test` consume immutable accepted `SceneView` data;
     5	hit testing requires the real `KernelResources` clip implementation and a
     6	caller work controller. Controlled bounds/source variants and hit testing
     7	charge visited edges/shapes and observe cancellation. `element_at_offset`
     8	selects the narrowest half-open source span, with later painter order winning
     9	ties. Slot enumeration uses accepted `SceneView::shape_id`, including
    10	zero-edge shapes, and inherits its generation/scene/owner validation.
    11	
    12	Scene publication assigns source spans on `ShapeInput` before
    13	`SceneBuilder::append_shape`. `source_assign` therefore modifies only an
    14	unpublished input; published spans remain immutable. Shapes are reached with
    15	accepted generation-checked handles. The safe allocation adapter records
    16	caller-owned capacity with shared `ChargeLedger` leases stored beside their
    17	buffers; the shared ledger is the sole lease registry. It does not claim raw
    18	allocator hooks, allocator metadata, or RSS. `reserve_table` builds a charged
    19	replacement while old storage remains live and transfers values only after
    20	admission succeeds. The old Vec capacity must already have a live ledger lease;
    21	keep that lease until replacement returns, then release it. The returned lease
    22	owns the new capacity until that buffer leaves the job.
    23	The adapter enforces the legacy 65,536 active-record bound and rejects leases
    24	from another tracking scope.
    25	
    26	The mixed original measurement fixture still requires coordinator composition
    27	with the concrete decoder/reference index, clip-copy producer, and raster
    28	output. Those integration assertions are retained in the work-order coverage
    29	record; they are not claimed as passed here.

